{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>No elohim.</b> As the Targum renders: \"in whom there is no need\" — had there been need in them, there would not have been doubled jealousy as now (Sifrei)." "<b>Recently come from near.</b> Even the nations were not accustomed to them — a nation that saw them would say, \"This is a Jewish idol.\"" "<b>Your fathers did not sha'arum.</b> They did not fear them — their hair did not stand on end because of them, for it is the way of a person's hair to stand from fear; thus it is expounded in Sifrei. And one may further explain <b>sha'arum</b> in the sense of ״וּשְׂעִירִים יְרַקְּדוּ שָׁם״ (Isaiah 13:21) — שְׂעִירִים are demons; your fathers did not make these שְׂעִירִים."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:15.588884883Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}